WEBVTT

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:10.070
We're goin' to the mansion?!

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:14.020
I know what's going to happen, 
and I have to stop it!

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:15.850
She's drawn to me, which means—

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:18.080
If you say we gotta use you as bait,

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.480
I'm gonna bite off one of your fingers!

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.870
The old hag and Ram and everyone 
else already got swallowed up!

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:28.460
I'd be a disgrace if I let it get you, too!

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:32.210
The shadow... swallowed up all of them?

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:36.080
Yeah.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:39.780
The whole ground was engulfed by the 
shadow before I even realized it.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:45.140
If Ram hadn't sent me flying with 
her wind, it would've gotten me, too.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.460
So Ram and Ryuzu-san were just...

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:49.650
And Otto...

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:52.400
And Emilia, too?

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:00.490
Damn it! Why now, of all times?!

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:02.620
Who's there?!

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.000
What kind of joke is this?

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.660
I was hopin' you wouldn't have to see this.

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:13.020
Are those clones of Ryuzu-san?

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.470
Don't worry about them.

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:17.070
They ain't her.

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:19.010
They're empty on the inside.

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:22.010
What are you planning to do?

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:25.140
What do you think?

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:29.580
We're gonna bust through with 
sheer numbers and crush it!

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.080
I love you.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:48.750
There you are!

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:54.510
Wait!

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:00.890
Go!

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:20.990
I love you.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:22.620
Shut up...

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:25.320
I love you. I love you. I love you.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:26.380
Shut up!

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:28.780
I love you. I love you. I love you.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:30.150
Subaru-kun...

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:33.200
Don't you dare call me that!

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:34.170
I love you. I love you. I love you.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.650
Cut the crap!

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:37.350
I love you. I love you. I love you.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:38.380
The first real "I love you" I was 
given in this world was so powerful,

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:40.490
I love you. I love you. I love you.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:43.870
it made me think a loser like me 
could actually become a hero!

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.870
I love you. I love you. I love you.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:46.910
The number one and number two places 
in my heart are already taken!

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:46.910
I love you. I love you. I love you.

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:48.850
There's no room in here for you!

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:51.730
I love you. I love you. I love you.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.730
Compared to you,

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:54.980
I'd have an easier time loving Echidna 
or any of the other witches!

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:07.550
I love you. I love you. I love you.

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:10.180
Love me. Love me.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:11.800
Love me.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:15.510
Love me. Love me. Love me.

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:18.740
Love me. Love me. Love me.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:21.140
Love me. Love me.

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:23.550
This... isn't death.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:26.940
Love me. Love me. Love me.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:28.340
The shadow is surrounding me...
engulfing me...

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:32.070
Love me. Love me. Love me.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:33.510
It's just... going to keep 
loving me... forever?

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:38.220
Love me. Love me. Love me. Love me. Love me.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.460
Petra's handkerchief...

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:41.570
Love me. Love me. Love me.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:45.360
Love me. Love me. Love me.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:46.970
Did Echidna... know this was going to happen?!

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:51.620
Love me. Love me. Love me. Love me. Love me.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:56.000
Love me. Love me. Love me. Love me.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:57.080
That damn witch!

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.440
Love me. Love me. Love me. Love me.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:00.760
Love me.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:39.360
I... swear...

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:43.800
I'm going... to save you.

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:58.580
I made it back.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.320
Emilia!

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:06.770
What?

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:14.670
Why am I shaking?

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.500
I can't... actually be...

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:26.550
Emi...lia...

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.140
Subaru?

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:33.890
Where...

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:37.040
Wait, I was just...

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:40.230
Subaru?

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:43.340
Why...

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:47.740
do you look like you're in so much pain?

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:01.140
It's all right. It's all right, Subaru.

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:03.270
I'm right here, see?

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:05.340
I'm right here.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:10.800
So...

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:14.080
You were supposed to help Emilia-sama, 
but you only caused trouble for her.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.310
Why are you even alive?

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:17.720
After you came in hoping to help me,

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:20.570
it's really a shame you got 
so worried that you started crying.

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:23.630
Emilia-tan, you're gonna make me cry again.

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:27.390
But you're always the one helping me.

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:31.100
So a part of me is relieved 
that you let me see

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:32.530
this weaker side of you.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:39.460
I'd rather not let you see 
that side of me, though.

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:41.350
Huh? Why not?

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:46.100
Because I only want you to see the part 
of me that's trying to look good.

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:51.260
I want you to forget that I'm 
actually a weak, helpless loser.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:54.640
Hey! I'm not going to hate you just because

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:57.060
you showed me a moment of weakness!

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:01.060
Hah. That pride isn't very convincing 
after you've just bawled your eyes out.

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:04.070
Do you have to rain on my 
parade every single time?!

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:08.100
Now, now. Ram-san's attitude is 
just how she shows she's worried.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:17.550
Yeah, I wasn't sure what was 
gonna happen for a minute,

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:20.010
but I'm glad ya made it back all right.

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:22.340
I guess a little breeze won't knock 
the gafgalon fruit off the tree,

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:24.380
and that ain't nothin' to sneeze at!

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:26.370
Ow!

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:28.550
Wait... that's it?

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:30.760
Huh?

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:34.970
<i>Well, if nothing else, 
Garfiel isn't hostile right now.</i>

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:37.640
<i>The trial didn't break Emilia's spirit,</i>

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:39.730
<i>and Garfiel is still maintaining 
his neutral stance.</i>

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:43.100
<i>This is the best starting 
point I've had so far.</i>

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:47.690
<i>Now I just need to work out what 
I can test, and what I can bring back.</i>

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:49.030
<i>I have to make use of this the best I can.</i>

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:54.200
Ram, there's something 
I want to talk to you about.

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:55.240
Pervert.

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:58.040
You're jumping to conclusions 
<i>and</i> making me sound bad!

00:07:58.040 --> 00:07:58.850
Hmph.

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:01.760
For one thing, I've never 
looked at you in that way!

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:04.210
True. You usually look much more vague.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:08.960
What is it you want to ask of me?

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:11.790
It's about Garfiel.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:14.150
I'm about to do something behind his back,

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:17.170
and there's a good chance 
he'll try to interfere.

00:08:17.170 --> 00:08:20.060
So I want you to keep him here.

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:23.390
I don't like that look in your eyes, Barusu.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:25.020
Get over your weird suspicions, would you?

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:27.180
Very well, then.

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:29.160
Thanks. I appreciate it.

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:30.300
Ten favors in return will do.

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:31.610
That's a lot!

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:39.940
<i>When I was inside that shadow, 
I merged with many consciousnesses.</i>

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:42.850
<i>Those were probably her victims' memories.</i>

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:45.110
<i>It's all disjointed fragments,</i>

00:08:45.110 --> 00:08:49.780
<i>but I was able to bring back 
more than my own life is worth.</i>

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:52.210
<i>Now all that's left is to 
verify those memories.</i>

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:56.180
Found it.

00:09:46.280 --> 00:09:49.860
Is this... Ryuzu-san?

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:56.570
I never expected you to discover this only 
half a day after arriving here, Young Su.

00:09:58.520 --> 00:10:00.550
It was the memory.

00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:02.740
The memory of someone who was 
swallowed up by the Witch of Envy,

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:05.510
someone who knew of this place.

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:11.330
Is the girl on the left the one 
who led me here this afternoon?

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:14.470
That is unlikely.

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:18.270
This girl is one of the guards 
assigned to this place.

00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:21.350
It was another who met you in the forest.

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:23.960
One of the Sanctuary's eyes, nothing more.

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:26.310
There's something I want to ask you.

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:30.060
After that, I'd like to request 
your help, if possible.

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:32.860
I shall not ignore your request, Young Su,

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:35.640
Apostle of Greed.

00:10:36.390 --> 00:10:37.320
That is...

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:41.700
what has been written in the 
contract that binds us,

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:43.420
the copies of Ryuzu Meyer.

00:10:48.590 --> 00:10:50.750
She seems awfully attached to me...

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:57.670
You do know who is responsible for 
creating this place, do you not?

00:10:57.860 --> 00:11:01.530
I think it was the Witch of Greed,
 Echidna, right?

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:05.430
Yes, this is a land built 
by said witch's hand,

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:09.820
an experimental facility meant 
to fulfill said witch's dream.

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:12.440
What was she experimenting on?

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:15.440
Can you not see it right in front of you?

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:21.910
Was there not a girl who looked just like 
me trapped within the magic crystal?

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:25.780
That was the true, the first, Ryuzu Meyer.

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:31.040
All the other Ryuzus, including 
myself, are copies of her.

00:11:31.720 --> 00:11:33.120
We are imitations.

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:39.210
Does knowing that I am an imitation 
change how you see me?

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:43.370
I don't know.

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:46.520
I'd really like to say that it doesn't.

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:47.310
I would, but...

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:52.640
How kind you are, Young Su.

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:56.110
Our replica bodies are built upon

00:11:56.110 --> 00:12:00.290
cores of artificial od that 
has been produced by magic.

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:03.520
Those cores are wrapped in 
mana and given physical form,

00:12:03.520 --> 00:12:05.430
resulting in these bodies.

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:09.730
Wait, you're talking about 
literally creating life!

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:13.580
Why the heck would she do 
an experiment like that?

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:17.040
To add something to those bodies, obviously.

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:21.460
Specifically, to add personalities, 
memories, and knowledge...

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:23.180
In other words, a soul.

00:12:23.770 --> 00:12:28.350
She filled Ryuzu Meyer's 
body with her own being,

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:30.920
and each time a body perished,

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:35.300
she would make a new vessel 
to inherit its soul,

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:36.650
which would make her...

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:39.860
...basically immortal.

00:12:41.510 --> 00:12:43.580
So that's it!

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:46.570
That's why she kept acting 
so familiar with me!

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:51.100
<i>My Return by Death makes me 
basically immortal, too.</i>

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:54.380
<i>Was she just happy to find a kindred spirit?</i>

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:58.170
So was Echidna's experiment a success?

00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:02.410
No, Echidna's soul was not inherited.

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:07.140
The witch's plans only came 
to pass in an imperfect form.

00:13:07.350 --> 00:13:08.980
An imperfect form?

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:11.980
Ryuzu Meyer was an insufficient vessel

00:13:11.980 --> 00:13:15.250
to house the Witch of Greed.

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:18.860
And she couldn't have figured 
that out before she tried it?

00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:22.920
After the witch's death, this facility remains,

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:26.020
and more copies continue to be produced.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:28.320
Since our bodies are made of mana,

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:33.660
our saving grace is that we require 
no resources to survive.

00:13:34.890 --> 00:13:37.360
Looks like you're drinking tea, though.

00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:39.250
This is merely a hobby of mine.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:44.130
An individual quirk that 
I acquired over my long life.

00:13:45.820 --> 00:13:49.760
I was one of the first four copies made,

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:52.260
400 years ago now.

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:56.470
I was given the wisdom and 
personality to manage

00:13:56.470 --> 00:13:58.770
the ever-increasing copies, 
as well as the Sanctuary.

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:00.780
You were created that way?

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:03.230
I did suffer at first.

00:14:03.550 --> 00:14:06.370
I had no memories, only a job to do.

00:14:06.850 --> 00:14:10.180
I know not how many years passed before

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:13.950
I truly felt as if I were alive...

00:14:15.800 --> 00:14:18.040
Now, do not look so sad.

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:24.000
In my own way, I have come to find 
significance in fulfilling my purpose.

00:14:24.550 --> 00:14:28.590
Okay, and what did you mean by 
"Apostle of Greed" earlier?

00:14:28.980 --> 00:14:35.350
Put simply, it refers to the one who has the 
right to command us copies of Ryuzu Meyer.

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:41.520
Did the witch not bestow upon you a symbol 
of her apostlehood in the graveyard?

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:43.430
What kind of symbol?

00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:47.940
A part of her body, such as a 
strand of hair or a fingernail.

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:50.860
Wait, the Chidna tea?!

00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:52.200
Chidna tea?

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:56.590
She got me to drink her bodily fluids 
cleverly disguised as tea, twice.

00:14:56.590 --> 00:14:59.210
So you ingested a part of the witch.

00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:02.680
All joking aside, that surely must be it.

00:15:02.680 --> 00:15:06.460
That brat! What the hell did she make me drink?!

00:15:09.490 --> 00:15:10.800
Wait...

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:14.430
If the right to command the copies 
is what makes someone her apostle...

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:17.470
Did Garfiel enter the graveyard 
and undergo the trial, too?

00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:27.320
Ryuzu-san...

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:32.040
Don't tell Garfiel that 
I'm an Apostle of Greed,

00:15:32.510 --> 00:15:34.530
or that we've been in touch.

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:37.950
Young Gar certainly would have 
something to say if he knew

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:40.500
that a relative of his was 
meeting with his lover.

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:44.430
That was incredibly mean, plus it 
would make me incredibly sinful!

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:47.260
But, yeah, I guess we're okay, then.

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:49.910
I'll probably need your 
help again in the future.

00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:51.130
I hope I can count on you.

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:54.760
Do as you please. I cannot defy you.

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:56.970
Should you need a Garfiel ward, or a hug pillow—

00:15:56.970 --> 00:16:01.080
Could you stop making me sound like 
some guy who's eternally frustrated?!

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:04.450
I'll need you to keep up 
the good work as an eye.

00:16:11.850 --> 00:16:13.530
Thanks, Ryuzu-san.

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:19.810
By the way, you said the original surname 
was Meyer, but yours is Bilma, right?

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:20.750
Where'd that come from?

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:26.500
To go by the name "Ryuzu" is the 
duty that has been instilled in me.

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:31.130
Therefore, we must express our 
individuality in other ways,

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:35.250
such as hobbies, preferences... and names.

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:37.660
Say, Young Su...

00:16:39.510 --> 00:16:44.070
If you do not mind, would you ask 
me the same question again...

00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:47.080
after tomorrow?

00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:56.870
I need to get everyone safely 
back to the village somehow.

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:03.420
<i>I don't want to go through that again.</i>

00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:06.980
Subaru? What are you doing out here?

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:12.110
Hey... it's a real shock when you 
act super-duper spooked like that.

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:15.750
Super-duper? Who says that 
in this day and age?

00:17:15.750 --> 00:17:17.740
I guess I was worried for nothing.

00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:20.730
I wasn't doing anything worth worrying about.

00:17:20.730 --> 00:17:22.470
Everything's fine.

00:17:31.930 --> 00:17:35.750
You almost look like a fairy, Emilia-tan.

00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:39.600
Hey! You shouldn't say mean 
things like that about someone!

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:41.160
Even I can get angry, you know.

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:42.580
It was supposed to be a compliment!

00:17:42.880 --> 00:17:45.830
Fairies are a type of evil spirit, aren't they?

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:47.730
You won't fool me into thinking 
that's a compliment!

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:50.840
Another pick-up line foiled 
by the cultural barrier!

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:55.940
Anyway, what're you doing walking 
around out here so late at night?

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:59.430
If Puck were here, he'd tell 
you that's bad for your skin.

00:17:59.430 --> 00:18:03.780
I guess, um... I have no excuse for that.

00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:06.340
I just haven't been able to sleep since then,

00:18:06.340 --> 00:18:08.850
so I went for a walk to feel 
the night breeze for a bit.

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:12.310
Because you're worried about the trial?

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:13.660
It's not that.

00:18:14.410 --> 00:18:16.960
No... maybe it is.

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:21.050
But I'm not entirely sure what it is myself.

00:18:21.050 --> 00:18:24.540
I was walking around hoping 
to figure it out... I guess.

00:18:26.170 --> 00:18:27.830
I really wish...

00:18:28.590 --> 00:18:30.540
Puck was here.

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:37.620
I guess, no matter where I go, 
I'll always be a pinch-hitter.

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:38.770
Huh?

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:43.470
You're amazing, Emilia.

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:46.360
No one would blame you for 
wanting to run away from this.

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:49.730
But you face it head-on without 
backing down. I respect that.

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:53.480
Wh-What brought this on all of a sudden?

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:55.120
It's not sudden.

00:18:55.560 --> 00:18:59.740
I've always thought that. I just 
couldn't say it until now.

00:19:00.210 --> 00:19:01.450
Subaru...

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:05.640
I don't know how much help I can be to you,

00:19:05.640 --> 00:19:08.200
but I'll say what I feel out loud.

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:10.200
You're gonna be fine, Emilia.

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:11.460
I know you'll get it done.

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:15.170
I'm on your side.

00:19:17.350 --> 00:19:19.360
Yeah. Thank you.

00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:23.740
Really, you've given me so much courage.

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:33.310
Natsuki-san, you're back?

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:36.150
You were gone for so long. 
I was worried about you.

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:38.780
I thought you'd wandered into 
the forest and gotten lost.

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:41.720
What are you, an overprotective mother?

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:44.280
At least let me be the father.

00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:48.880
Natsuki-san, I know you've 
had a hard time lately,

00:19:48.880 --> 00:19:51.130
but you can always talk to me if it'll help.

00:19:51.130 --> 00:19:53.400
This guy says the weirdest 
things in his sleep. Gross.

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:56.710
Is that what you say to someone 
who was worried about you?!

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:02.400
Just be quiet and sleep.

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:06.860
If your little outbursts get the villagers 
riled up, we're all in for it.

00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:09.670
Um... I didn't mean that as a joke.

00:20:09.670 --> 00:20:12.030
I know, I know.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:16.390
That's exactly why I can't tell you.

00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:19.770
<i>I'm going alone.</i>

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:24.330
<i>Emilia,</i>

00:20:24.330 --> 00:20:27.880
<i>I'm going back to Roswaal's mansion 
to take care of something.</i>

00:20:27.880 --> 00:20:32.040
<i>It's something I can't tell Ram, 
Roswaal, or the villagers about.</i>

00:20:32.860 --> 00:20:35.150
<i>So you don't need to worry about anything.</i>

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:37.080
<i>I'll be back as soon as I'm done.</i>

00:20:38.940 --> 00:20:41.340
I'm in a world where it's assumed 
that I'll redo everything,

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:44.030
so it's not like it even makes sense to do this.

00:20:45.950 --> 00:20:47.780
Let's go, Patrasche.

00:20:52.490 --> 00:20:54.490
<i>Even if this world will disappear,</i>

00:20:54.490 --> 00:20:56.850
<i>even if I'll end up leaving it behind,</i>

00:20:57.280 --> 00:20:59.630
<i>I don't want Emilia to look sad.</i>

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:02.570
<i>My goal is to win at the Roswaal mansion.</i>

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:05.980
<i>I need to figure out exactly 
what's going on there.</i>

00:21:06.390 --> 00:21:09.360
<i>If I don't know that, there's no
 way I can deal with it.</i>

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:12.580
<i>But if I can find out, I can 
even ask Echidna for help.</i>

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:15.320
I'll do as many tests as I have to.

00:21:15.320 --> 00:21:18.130
That's something only I can do.

00:21:21.450 --> 00:21:24.300
Hah! So much energy first 
thing in the morning.

00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:28.190
That's one damn gutsy ground 
dragon ya got there.

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:32.120
There seems to be a misunderstanding 
between you and me.

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:34.730
A misunderstanding? Like hell there is!

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:40.110
You and your witch stench are goin' 
out to do somethin' evil, aren't ya?

00:21:40.640 --> 00:21:42.570
I won't deny smelling bad,

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:44.470
but why bring it up now?

00:21:45.680 --> 00:21:48.090
You didn't say anything about it yesterday.

00:21:49.560 --> 00:21:52.050
Looks like that was an 
inconvenient question for you.

00:21:52.420 --> 00:21:54.920
It's written all over your face, Garfiel.

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:57.690
Stop it.

00:21:57.690 --> 00:22:01.090
Don't go makin' me more pissed 
off than I already am.

00:22:03.700 --> 00:22:05.890
Don't even think about it, ground dragon!

00:22:05.890 --> 00:22:08.900
One move, and your precious 
master gets smashed!

00:22:13.010 --> 00:22:14.790
What're you smirking about?!

00:22:15.500 --> 00:22:18.900
You... You're so easy... to read...

00:22:18.900 --> 00:22:19.640
Huh?!

00:22:20.120 --> 00:22:24.860
Now I've got a good idea of what 
gets a reaction out of you,

00:22:25.490 --> 00:22:27.680
and what makes you mad.

00:22:36.770 --> 00:22:39.370
You bastard! You were testing me?!

00:22:40.160 --> 00:22:41.730
You're insane!

00:22:41.730 --> 00:22:45.060
What the hell d'you think you're 
riskin' your life for?!

00:22:45.060 --> 00:22:50.300
If my life was enough, it'd go pretty 
damn well with the end result.

00:22:51.860 --> 00:22:54.680
Keep an open mind and let 
me off the hook, would you?

00:22:54.680 --> 00:22:56.880
If I let you go now,

00:22:56.880 --> 00:22:59.480
can you guarantee you aren't gonna 
do anything bad to us later?

00:22:59.820 --> 00:23:02.100
I won't betray Emilia,

00:23:02.100 --> 00:23:04.600
and I won't do anything bad to the Sanctuary.

00:23:04.600 --> 00:23:05.650
Trust me.

00:23:07.660 --> 00:23:11.660
Garfiel, I know you're hiding something.

00:23:11.660 --> 00:23:13.620
But I'm going to find out what it is.

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:14.870
I swear it.

00:23:15.100 --> 00:23:15.890
Shut up!

00:23:15.890 --> 00:23:19.580
So long as I don't give up,
 there are no secrets.

00:23:19.580 --> 00:23:21.740
You'd be wasting your time trying to stop me.

00:23:21.740 --> 00:23:25.000
What do you wanna do to this place?! To us?!

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:28.870
I told you what my goal is: to help Emilia.

00:23:28.870 --> 00:23:31.690
I have no intention of doing 
any harm to the Sanctuary.

00:23:31.690 --> 00:23:35.120
I might put you guys through 
some hardship, but I want to help you all.

00:23:35.120 --> 00:23:37.210
Who the hell do you think you are?!

00:23:37.210 --> 00:23:40.520
You don't know shit about this place, 
or the old hag, or anyone else!

00:23:40.520 --> 00:23:42.640
What I don't know, I'm going to learn.

00:23:42.640 --> 00:23:45.150
I consider that the reason I'm doing this.

00:23:45.370 --> 00:23:48.030
What the hell are you gonna accomplish 
with that uppity bullshit?!

00:23:48.300 --> 00:23:51.470
You have no idea what pain 
or suffering even are!

00:23:51.470 --> 00:23:53.530
Quit runnin' your damn mouth as if you do!

00:23:53.930 --> 00:23:54.950
I do know.

00:23:57.490 --> 00:23:59.540
I know hell.

00:24:02.760 --> 00:24:05.620
I've seen it many times.

00:24:18.870 --> 00:24:22.060
I'm the only one who needs to know hell.

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:28.270
That's what I'm here for.

00:24:28.270 --> 00:24:31.280
<b>I Know Hell</b>

00:24:34.260 --> 00:24:37.950
We should leave the mansion and 
take cover in the village for now?

00:24:38.660 --> 00:24:40.400
This is what you wish of us?

00:24:40.400 --> 00:24:41.930
Yeah, if you would.

00:24:41.930 --> 00:24:44.710
Sorry to make you deal with this, 
but I know you can handle it.

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:47.720
Goodness, what a pick-up line.

00:24:47.720 --> 00:24:51.990
You certainly know how to win 
a maid's heart, Subaru-sama.

00:24:51.990 --> 00:24:54.590
Me, too! I agree with her!

00:24:54.860 --> 00:24:56.650
Thanks for the protective charm.

00:24:56.650 --> 00:25:00.930
It really helped, though maybe 
not in the way you intended.

00:25:01.140 --> 00:25:04.350
Really? I was useful to you?

00:25:04.350 --> 00:25:06.520
Yeah. You saved my life...

00:25:06.520 --> 00:25:08.620
Well, that's not totally accurate,

00:25:08.620 --> 00:25:09.820
but that's how helpful it was.

00:25:10.080 --> 00:25:11.450
I'm so glad!

00:25:11.450 --> 00:25:13.990
In that case, you can thank me with one date!

00:25:14.400 --> 00:25:15.320
Got it.

00:25:15.320 --> 00:25:18.280
It'll be an honor to be your first date.

00:25:18.280 --> 00:25:19.370
I'll get fired up for it.

00:25:19.620 --> 00:25:21.130
That's a promise!

00:25:21.720 --> 00:25:24.420
Well, I'm going to go get ready!

00:25:26.750 --> 00:25:29.710
<i>Let's be sure to make more promises like that.</i>

00:25:30.680 --> 00:25:32.600
She is a very good girl.

00:25:33.760 --> 00:25:34.540
Yeah.

00:25:36.230 --> 00:25:41.410
Take care of Rem, Petra, Patrasche...
 and yourself, too.

00:25:41.410 --> 00:25:44.270
I'll join you as soon as I can.

00:25:44.660 --> 00:25:50.030
I will eagerly await the moment you 
join us along with Beatrice-sama.

00:25:56.800 --> 00:25:58.860
You're finally here, I suppose.

00:25:59.500 --> 00:26:03.700
I'm here for a different reason than last time.

00:26:04.270 --> 00:26:06.210
Do as you wish.

00:26:06.640 --> 00:26:09.330
It's all quite ironic either way, I suppose.

00:26:10.710 --> 00:26:13.500
The end of a contract that 
lasted a long, long time...

00:26:13.920 --> 00:26:16.360
By bringing an end to the end of the end,

00:26:16.360 --> 00:26:19.050
I will truly be set free this time.

00:26:19.650 --> 00:26:20.850
Of course...

00:26:22.480 --> 00:26:25.260
The fact that it has to be with you

00:26:25.260 --> 00:26:28.680
makes it an ending far too 
ironic for me, I suppose.
